or (at your option) any later version (see LICENSE).

As an exception, the files that NativeForge copies into the APKs and web pages
it exports are also available under the zlib license below, so that programs
written with NativeForge can be distributed under any license. These files are:

  * runtime-template/            (the host app that exported programs run in)
  * feature/runner/              (program hosts and the native shim, nativeforge_shim.c)
  * core/export/src/main/resources/io/nativeforge/core/export/web/
                                 (the web page, WASI runtime and terminal of web exports)

The org.libsdl.app Java files in feature/runner/src/main/java are part of SDL
and are already under the zlib license.

